From ba767d6f6dbaedca5cf776fd3ebf54cb40426df1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 03:42:24 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 198/215] fix: e_svoTI_SpecularAmplifier now reaches ray traced
 pixels too

Energy audit error 3 / E4. Every VOXEL specular pixel is multiplied by
e_svoTI_SpecularAmplifier inside the cone trace (CommonSVO.cfi:1323-1328,
SvoParamsSpecular.w). An RT pixel never saw it, because the g-data write at the
end of ConeTracePS overwrites the traced colour wholesale and the ShadePass
rebuilds it from scratch. The amplifier is a per-level Total Illumination
setting, so on a level that tamed it to 0.3 the RT reflections sat a flat 1/0.3
brighter than the voxel reflections next to them, with a step at the
e_svoTI_RT_MinGloss knee where the two halves of the picture meet.

ShadePS now applies the same value in the same units, right after the emissive
and before the fog, the writer clamp and the exposure divide.

To be explicit about what this is: the amplifier is a pure artistic gain applied
to what is otherwise a radiance. A PHYSICALLY EXACT LEVEL SHOULD SET
e_svoTI_SpecularAmplifier TO 1. The multiply is here so that RT and voxel pixels
agree with each other, not because the gain itself is correct. IsRtHitShadingActive
already requires the amplifier to be non-zero, so this can never blank the pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SCUvWGLCsqzm3VNMzp4uiS
---
 .../HWScripts/CryFX/Total_Illumination.cfx        | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Total_Illumination.cfx b/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Total_Illumination.cfx
index 61ba026e..b644ef87 100644
--- a/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Total_Illumination.cfx
+++ b/Engine/Shaders/HWScripts/CryFX/Total_Illumination.cfx
@@ -2102,6 +2102,21 @@ pixoutShade ShadePS(vtxOutWPOS IN)
 		// Neo's borrowed-hue trick for a scalar-only atlas, and we carry a real hue now.
 		acc += fwdAttribs.custom.Emittance * vEmmTint * PS_HDR_RANGE_ADAPT_MAX;
 
+		// rt stage 4A, energy audit error 3 / E4. Every VOXEL specular pixel is multiplied by
+		// e_svoTI_SpecularAmplifier inside the cone trace (CommonSVO.cfi:1323-1328,
+		// SvoParamsSpecular.w); an RT pixel never saw it, because the g-data write at the end of
+		// ConeTracePS overwrites the traced colour wholesale. So on a level tuned with the
+		// amplifier at, say, 0.3 - and it is a per-level Total Illumination setting, not a
+		// constant - the RT reflections sat a flat 1/0.3 brighter than the voxel reflections
+		// beside them, with a visible step at the e_svoTI_RT_MinGloss knee where the two meet.
+		// Applied here, on the same value and in the same units, so the two halves of the picture
+		// carry the same gain.
+		//
+		// It is a pure artistic gain on what is otherwise a radiance: A PHYSICALLY EXACT LEVEL
+		// SHOULD SET e_svoTI_SpecularAmplifier TO 1. This multiply exists to keep RT and voxel
+		// pixels consistent with each other, not because the gain is right.
+		acc *= SvoParamsSpecular.w;
+
 		if (SVO_ShadeParams0.y) // debug: flat albedo
 			acc = fwdAttribs.albedo;
 
